  "pitch": "Escape to Surfside Beach, Texas, a relaxed coastal gem perfect for a laid-back couple seeking good food, scenic beaches, and unhurried exploration. With no early mornings and a pace designed around leisurely dining and natural attractions, this 14-day retreat honors both Alice's preference for a slower start to each day and Bob's love of excellent meals paired with easy-going exploration. The Polynesian Ocean Front Hotel puts you steps from the water, and every day flows naturally from breakfast through beachside lunch to evening dining, all without the rush or pressure of an overpacked schedule.\n\nYour itinerary weaves together the best of the coastal region's offerings across two weeks of discovery. Days 1–3 ease you in with Surfside Beach itself, the Yucca Avenue Public Beach Access, and local flavor at La Casona Tex Mex and La Michoacana Meat Market. Days 4–7 expand your horizons with Jasmine Park, Surfside Jetty County Park, Quintana Beach County Park, Freeport Bryan Beach, and Brazoria Beach, each offering a different slice of the shoreline and surrounding parkland. By Days 8–14, you'll venture inland to Lake Jackson Recreation Center, Oyster Creek Municipal Park, and the Justin Hurst Wildlife Management Area, before returning to beloved beach spots like Surfside Beach Jetty Point and concluding with a final morning at Quintana Beach County Park and Surfside Beach itself.\n\nThe Polynesian Ocean Front Hotel ($57 per night, $798 total for your stay) serves as your home base throughout, offering oceanfront convenience and comfort. Every morning begins at 10:00 with breakfast at Beach Front Deck Bar and Grill—no rushing—followed by activities that range from beach walks to park exploration, then lunch at the consistently excellent Salty Pelican Surfside Beach. Dinner returns you to Salty Pelican each evening, a restaurant perfectly suited to both Alice's desire for quality dining and Bob's appreciation for relaxed, no-fuss meals. The gentle pacing ensures you'll never feel hurried, and the three-activity-per-day maximum keeps each day manageable and genuinely enjoyable.\n\nThis is a trip built for connection, good food, and the unhurried pleasures of a Texas coastal escape. You'll discover hidden parks, savor fresh seafood and local fare, and spend two full weeks exactly as you want to spend them—together, well-fed, and completely at ease. Pack your appetite and your patience for long beach strolls; Surfside Beach awaits.",
